 "notes": {
  "forAnalyst": "The editorial side of a storefront: pages, blog posts, blocks, menus and the theme itself, edited per store. It is what a marketing team changes without a release.",
  "forArchitect": "Barely a database module — two entities, both about menus. Everything else lives in blob storage, which is why it depends on Assets **and** on both storage providers, and why its content is deployed rather than migrated. Three index builders make pages searchable alongside products. Content is per store, so Store is a required dependency.",
  "forDeveloper": "Work through the content API per store and content type rather than touching blobs, and remember that the storefront reads themes and pages at runtime — a change is visible without a rebuild, and a bad change is visible just as fast. Menus are the only part with relational structure and its own change events.",
  "owns": [
   "MenuLinkListEntity",
   "MenuLinkEntity"
  ],
  "reachForItWhen": [
   "Pages, blocks, menus or theme files are the thing being managed",
   "Editorial content has to be searchable next to catalog data",
   "A storefront needs per-store content without a deployment"
  ],
  "doNotReachForItWhen": [
   "You need structured product data — that is Catalog, with a schema behind it",
   "You expect database migrations to move your content: it is files in blob storage",
   "You want a page builder experience — that is a separate module on top of this one"
  ]
 },
